    <title>Useful</title>
    <updated>2026-11-18T00:36:31Z</updated>
    <link rel="alternate" href="https://positivitybriefing.com/#item-1" type="text/html"/>
    <content type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">A loose wooden chair joint can often be tightened by cleaning out old glue, applying fresh wood glue and clamping it firmly until dry; avoid forcing a wobbly joint.</div>
    </content>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <id>https://positivitybriefing.com/feed.atom#155c4a3148453a5ece6668746fc9409411fab728d24d13186b6ca7a15167e55a</id>
    <title>Hopeful</title>
    <updated>2026-11-18T00:36:31Z</updated>
    <link rel="alternate" href="https://positivitybriefing.com/#item-2" type="text/html"/>
    <content type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">During the Second World War, people in Britain organised community salvage drives for materials such as aluminium and paper, showing how local coordination could turn everyday discards into useful resources.</div>
    </content>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <id>https://positivitybriefing.com/feed.atom#1167c2ed383ae235969637d67e46e42e01a32a695eb21fad9841c6895f7a1513</id>
    <title>Action</title>
    <updated>2026-11-18T00:36:31Z</updated>
    <link rel="alternate" href="https://positivitybriefing.com/#item-3" type="text/html"/>
    <content type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">In under five minutes, check one kitchen drawer, return misplaced utensils to their proper places and remove any broken or duplicate items you already know you won’t use.</div>
    </content>
